    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0344" n="256" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg256"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr. Squiers.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-01-14"><hi rendition="#italic">January 14,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 319.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to former correspondence in
                    regard to the killing of E. A. Murray, I have to request that you will ask the
                    foreign office to advise you as to the result of the investigation which Mr.
                    Zaldo on November 9 last stated had been ordered “to find out what
                    responsibility there may be on the part of the police on duty at the police
                    headquarters of Puerto Principe.”</p>
                <p>You will inform the Department of the result of your inquiry.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. B. Loomis.</hi><lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
